      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:201611_St._Joseph%27s_Church_Beijing_exterior.jpg",
        "author": "Another Believer",
        "date": "2016-11-20",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected full western front and broad approach steps. Three deeply arched doors,heavy stone bases,two facade orders divided by a projecting cornice,central rose,paired round-headed upper side lights,slender vertical pale plaques and three domed/crossed towers. The central tower is higher;dark louver panels are not open air. Trees obscure side/rear body. Detailed Chinese inscriptions,statues and fine reliefs are simplified,not used as texture maps."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Joseph%27s_Cathedral,_Beijing_walls_1.JPG",
